{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976327-pyrokenesis","id":976327,"title":"Pyrokenesis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-25T20:42:08-07:00","id":976327,"title":"Pyrokenesis","content":"Well this is a mind sphere rote, I honestly don't understand how it works like, do I need to use it to do something like friction curse? or set someone on fire or drop lightning on some targets from the sky?<br /> That means I can't use kinetic energy of forces to lift a car or a person without mind? and if not, how exactly do you use forces knetic energy and levitation?<br /> I hope I could get an answer to all these questions anytime soon.<br /> Thanks in advance and love you guys &lt;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:44:33-07:00","id":976329,"title":"","content":"Its mind and forces..... read how did you do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T21:40:52-07:00","id":976344,"title":"","content":"Just because a book says needs mind doesn't mean it makes sense. That's ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T22:33:16-07:00","id":976360,"title":"","content":"To me, the reason that it needs Mind is the same reason you need Prime in some cases. It's a matter of &quot;cannot create from nothing&quot;. You convert your though processes into heat.<br /> Sure, you could go Forces only, converting one force into another. It's up to how you view your characters paradigm and how your character views magic.<br /> If your character is convinced that he needs a Mind component, you need a Mind component.<br /> It's like the Spirit talker that is convinced that all his Forces abilities stems not from him, but from the Elemental spirits he deals with. For him, he needs a conjunctional Spirit/Forces effect to create fire by making a deal with a fire elemental.<br /> <br /> At least that's my take on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T22:34:05-07:00","id":976361,"title":"","content":"Unless you're converting mental power/effort into fire, it doesn't need Mind. Although, if you aren't making it from mental power and you aren't making the fire from another Force, you need Prime 2 to create it from nowhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T23:12:03-07:00","id":976380,"title":"","content":"You could also summon fire from your sanctum's big furnace with conjunctional forces/correspondence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T23:49:02-07:00","id":976394,"title":"","content":"Oh, i suddenly had a horribly evil idea. A Mage who uses conjunctional Spirit/Forces to take spirits across the Gauntlet and convert the ephemera into forces, using spirits as fuel for his magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T03:32:54-07:00","id":976447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976327-pyrokenesis?p=976394#post976394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, i suddenly had a horribly evil idea. A Mage who uses conjunctional Spirit/Forces to take spirits across the Gauntlet and convert the ephemera into forces, using spirits as fuel for his magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not going to make you any friends...<br /> How would the difficulty be calculated for a move like that? Gauntlet rating? Sphere level? Both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T04:08:51-07:00","id":976457,"title":"","content":"I really didn't like this piece in HDYDT. At first I thought it was a way to create fire from the mind. Like a replacement for prime. <br /> <br /> But it isn't. You still need prime if the fire doesn't exist. So Mind is there pointlessly. Your paradigm should be a form of role play it shouldn't force you to add extra spheres that aren't needed. Especially when M20 reads that all Mages use the same rules, just don't tell the mages that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:42:30-07:00","id":976573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976327-pyrokenesis?p=976457#post976457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really didn't like this piece in HDYDT. At first I thought it was a way to create fire from the mind. Like a replacement for prime.<br /> <br /> But it isn't. You still need prime if the fire doesn't exist. So Mind is there pointlessly. Your paradigm should be a form of role play it shouldn't force you to add extra spheres that aren't needed. Especially when M20 reads that all Mages use the same rules, just don't tell the mages that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about the whole &quot;A bit of spirit&quot; part in M20. It suggests that any mage who's paradigm is spirits are the power behind magic may require the Spirit sphere in any magic they perform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:26:45-07:00","id":976601,"title":"","content":"&quot;A Bit of Spirit&quot; [HDYDT: p16] is an optional rule. When I first read that and Pyrokensis (and there was something else in HDYDT and it is slipping my mind) I thought it was kind of a neat idea to replace Prime with Mind or Spirit. I read it wrong, it isn't a replacement it is a tack-on (we will now all accept &quot;tack-on&quot; as a term). I may have been cool with that if it was a direct replacement, but with the counter that it does limit to your paradigm. For example a Pyrokineticist (idk, google liked the word... I will go with it) believes so much they create fire with their mind, they can no longer create it with prime. Which is kind of a cool concept, but not sure how much I would like it in practice.<br /> <br /> Even tho I really like that concept, it kind of goes against M20 p498 where they introduce the magick system.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ultimate irony of the Ascension War is that everyone\u2019s basically doing the same thing, yet they\u2019re killing one another over their impression of how and why they do it. <u>In game terms</u>, <u>all mages</u> <u>use the same rules</u>. The characters don\u2019t see it that way, but the players recognize that fact. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">This paragraph made my life a lot easier when trying to re-understand Mage (it has been 15 years, this is nothing like riding a bike... heck riding a bike is nothing like riding a bike, I think that phrase is broken). Paradigm is role-play, which is super important to this game system particularly, otherwise mages would be beyond powerful. So Paradigm is the mechanic that says what you believe you can do, but the spheres should be consistent (at least I feel) in how you can do it. This isn't to say you can't get super creative by using matter to make an object roll to you instead of forces to push it to you.<br /> <br /> Edit (My whole point I was going to come back to, but forgot): This is the only part in Mage I don't like. M20 seems pretty good with consistency, but there are a couple pieces in HDYDT that contradicts some core elements in M20. These are the two pieces I keep coming back to when talking about my one head-scratcher with M20. This seems unbalance to me, and maybe there is a piece I am missing, but because of someone's paradigm it makes Pyrokinetics 11.11% easier to counter magick that mage. When it should be the same rules, just the mage believes it is coming from a different place. Tho the flip side it does make it 11.11% harder to unweave it. <br /> <br /> I told my players if they want to add in other spheres (as long as it fits their paradigm) to make the pattern of the magick harder to undo, they may, but I don't require it for all their castings. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2900,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","user":"frostbyte000jm","date":". 09-26-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:06:50-07:00","id":976618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976327-pyrokenesis?p=976601#post976601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A Bit of Spirit&quot; [HDYDT: p16] is an optional rule. When I first read that and Pyrokensis (and there was something else in HDYDT and it is slipping my mind) I thought it was kind of a neat idea to replace Prime with Mind or Spirit. I read it wrong, it isn't a replacement it is a tack-on (we will now all accept &quot;tack-on&quot; as a term). I may have been cool with that if it was a direct replacement, but with the counter that it does limit to your paradigm. For example a Pyrokineticist (idk, google liked the word... I will go with it) believes so much they create fire with their mind, they can no longer create it with prime. Which is kind of a cool concept, but not sure how much I would like it in practice.<br /> <br /> Even tho I really like that concept, it kind of goes against M20 p498 where they introduce the magick system.<br /> [/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I don't think it would. Were I to run with the idea, I would say the Mind was being used to let you convert Willpower into fuel for the effect. That means the spell is inherently different than the standard summon quintessence variety. Mind is clearly doing something. HDYDT's problem is that it keeps adding spheres that don't actually do anything.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:28:14-07:00","id":976628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976327-pyrokenesis?p=976618#post976618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I don't think it would. Were I to run with the idea, I would say the Mind was being used to let you convert Willpower into fuel for the effect. That means the spell is inherently different than the standard summon quintessence variety. Mind is clearly doing something. HDYDT's problem is that it keeps adding spheres that don't actually do anything.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Like I mentioned if Mind replaced prime, instead of had to be tacked-on to the prime, forces spell, I may be cool with it. What you're saying sounds cool. But that isn't how it reads in HDYDT. <br /> <br /> I don't think Mind, forces, and using will in place of Q goes against M20 everyone uses the same rules. But adding Mind when it isn't needed does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:32:14-07:00","id":976631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976327-pyrokenesis?p=976628#post976628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I mentioned if Mind replaced prime, instead of had to be tacked-on to the prime, forces spell, I may be cool with it. What you're saying sounds cool. But that isn't how it reads in HDYDT.<br /> <br /> I don't think Mind, forces, and using will in place of Q goes against M20 everyone uses the same rules. But adding Mind when it isn't needed does.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you are right, HDYDT is completely against everything we were told. Might as well ask technomancers to use forces because their tools use electricity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:34:23-07:00","id":976634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976327-pyrokenesis?p=976601#post976601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A Bit of Spirit&quot; [HDYDT: p16] is an optional rule. When I first read that and Pyrokensis (and there was something else in HDYDT and it is slipping my mind) I thought it was kind of a neat idea to replace Prime with Mind or Spirit. I read it wrong, it isn't a replacement it is a tack-on (we will now all accept &quot;tack-on&quot; as a term). I may have been cool with that if it was a direct replacement, but with the counter that it does limit to your paradigm. For example a Pyrokineticist (idk, google liked the word... I will go with it) believes so much they create fire with their mind, they can no longer create it with prime. Which is kind of a cool concept, but not sure how much I would like it in practice.<br /> <br /> Even tho I really like that concept, it kind of goes against M20 p498 where they introduce the magick system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">This paragraph made my life a lot easier when trying to re-understand Mage (it has been 15 years, this is nothing like riding a bike... heck riding a bike is nothing like riding a bike, I think that phrase is broken). Paradigm is role-play, which is super important to this game system particularly, otherwise mages would be beyond powerful. So Paradigm is the mechanic that says what you believe you can do, but the spheres should be consistent (at least I feel) in how you can do it. This isn't to say you can't get super creative by using matter to make an object roll to you instead of forces to push it to you.<br /> <br /> Edit (My whole point I was going to come back to, but forgot): This is the only part in Mage I don't like. M20 seems pretty good with consistency, but there are a couple pieces in HDYDT that contradicts some core elements in M20. These are the two pieces I keep coming back to when talking about my one head-scratcher with M20. This seems unbalance to me, and maybe there is a piece I am missing, but because of someone's paradigm it makes Pyrokinetics 11.11% easier to counter magick that mage. When it should be the same rules, just the mage believes it is coming from a different place. Tho the flip side it does make it 11.11% harder to unweave it.<br /> <br /> I told my players if they want to add in other spheres (as long as it fits their paradigm) to make the pattern of the magick harder to undo, they may, but I don't require it for all their castings. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>I usually rule that Paradigm has a huge influence on what kind of things people can do with the Spheres. For example, if you're a Hermetic that believes that all forces are different and separate energies, then you would consider &quot;Darkness&quot; to be a different energy to &quot;light&quot; and as such, to change dark into light would require Forces 3, (while with Forces 2 you could move darkness around in the same way you might move fire around). If, however, you were a Etherite who bought into the theory of photons, then the concept of moving light is actually just moving photons to you, as such you can change light into dark with only Forces 2 since you're just moving photons around (but the very concept of moving &quot;darkness&quot; doesn't really make any kind of sense, so you can't do it).<br /> <br /> Another example is Entropy. If you see the world as inherently chaotic, and magic is just a way a mage justifies to themselves the illusion of order, as some Hollowers might think, then Entropy magic is about either returning things to chaos, or enforcing a form of order to them, so if you wanted to use Entropy to find the nearest escape route, they'd basically be creating themselves a route via random circumstance with Entropy 2. There is no &quot;perfect route&quot; because order is just an illusion, if they want it, they need to force it into being. This Hollower would, however be able to use Entropy 1 to recognise events which have lost this illusion, and thus are more likely succumb to chaotic influence, such as falling apart or degrading into nothingness.<br /> <br /> A Verbena who believes in Fate, however, would see the Entropy sphere from completely the opposite direction. To them there is inherent order and purpose for everyone, and all they need to do is listen out for natures call. To find an escape route would simply be an Entropy 1 effect, because they believe it is their fate to escape, and as such they only need to listen out to their fate and intuit the correct path. Entropy 2, then, would be about fighting against this fate, introducing unexpected things either to enhance or detract from your predetermined path.<br /> <br /> On the a complete tangent, a Virtual Adept would see Entropy as mere Statistical algorithms. To find an escape route would be to map out the quickest route to exit, and while the Verbena may intuit their exit, the Virtual Adept instead obtains a list of directions from their algorithm, which they must then follow or else become sub-optimal. Entropy 2 would allow them to influence aspects of their route by running the numbers and determining what actions will lead to what results, making their escape easier. They aren't really changing anything, as the Hollower would put it, instead they are just making the best possible decisions with the parameters they have at their disposal.<br /> <br /> I find that this can be done with all the spheres, with paradigm shaping out what it is that the mage believes is possible within their purview, and thus has different interpretations of what &quot;manipulating&quot; actually entails.<br /> <br /> A different example of paradigm affecting mechanics is in the case of a devoutly religious mage who believes that they are not casting magic, but rather acting as a conduit for the magic of their personal deity. So for the, magic isn't their will, but the will of their creator. This means that if such a mage were to botch their magic, they may consider it a sign that their deity is displeased with this activity and thus trying again would be a fools errand.<br /> <br /> Then there's the whole &quot;Science!&quot; thing that M20 brings up, which suggests that a Scientific paradigm would allow a Technomage to explain away Vulgar effects into coincidental ones so long as their effects stay in light with their theory and serves to demonstrate a new or old hypothesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:25:01-07:00","id":976659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976327-pyrokenesis?p=976634#post976634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I usually rule that Paradigm has a huge influence on what kind of things people can do with the Spheres. For example, if you're a Hermetic that believes that all forces are different and separate energies, then you would consider &quot;Darkness&quot; to be a different energy to &quot;light&quot; and as such, to change dark into light would require Forces 3, (while with Forces 2 you could move darkness around in the same way you might move fire around). If, however, you were a Etherite who bought into the theory of photons, then the concept of moving light is actually just moving photons to you, as such you can change light into dark with only Forces 2 since you're just moving photons around (but the very concept of moving &quot;darkness&quot; doesn't really make any kind of sense, so you can't do it).<br /> <br /> Another example is Entropy. If you see the world as inherently chaotic, and magic is just a way a mage justifies to themselves the illusion of order, as some Hollowers might think, then Entropy magic is about either returning things to chaos, or enforcing a form of order to them, so if you wanted to use Entropy to find the nearest escape route, they'd basically be creating themselves a route via random circumstance with Entropy 2. There is no &quot;perfect route&quot; because order is just an illusion, if they want it, they need to force it into being. This Hollower would, however be able to use Entropy 1 to recognise events which have lost this illusion, and thus are more likely succumb to chaotic influence, such as falling apart or degrading into nothingness.<br /> <br /> A Verbena who believes in Fate, however, would see the Entropy sphere from completely the opposite direction. To them there is inherent order and purpose for everyone, and all they need to do is listen out for natures call. To find an escape route would simply be an Entropy 1 effect, because they believe it is their fate to escape, and as such they only need to listen out to their fate and intuit the correct path. Entropy 2, then, would be about fighting against this fate, introducing unexpected things either to enhance or detract from your predetermined path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there is a certain amount of support for that. Alternate Spheres like Data and Dimensional Science exist because the mages who use them have very different views of the world. Things get hard to adjudicate if you push that too far, though. After all some of the Traditions don't think there's any kind of Conservation of Energy, or even any kind primal energy or firmament, so shouldn't some mages get to drop the Prime 2 requirement on manifesting something from nothing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:41:16-07:00","id":976666,"title":"","content":"In Guide to the Technocracy you had Psionic spheres. Where essentially you can declare 1-2 spheres 'psionic' spheres. From then on you can just use those spheres without any physical focus, but instead mental focus.<br /> <br /> Of course it implied the backlashes tended to have a nasty effect on your psyche, but who doesn't expect psychics to be a bit unhinged?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:52:48-07:00","id":976671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976327-pyrokenesis?p=976659#post976659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well there is a certain amount of support for that. Alternate Spheres like Data and Dimensional Science exist because the mages who use them have very different views of the world. Things get hard to adjudicate if you push that too far, though. After all some of the Traditions don't think there's any kind of Conservation of Energy, or even any kind primal energy or firmament, so shouldn't some mages get to drop the Prime 2 requirement on manifesting something from nothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, because Conservation of Energy could very easily involve Prime, since matter is not created nor destroyed, but simply take from or returned to prime.<br /> <br /> If however, they don't believe in Prime at all, then they probably don't have any dots in the Prime sphere and would have a very very hard time getting dots in Prime to start with, therefor, they cannot create matter or energy out of nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T14:28:08-07:00","id":976734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976327-pyrokenesis?p=976634#post976634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I usually rule that Paradigm has a huge influence on what kind of things people can do with the Spheres. For example, if you're a Hermetic that believes that all forces are different and separate energies, then you would consider &quot;Darkness&quot; to be a different energy to &quot;light&quot; and as such, to change dark into light would require Forces 3, (while with Forces 2 you could move darkness around in the same way you might move fire around). If, however, you were a Etherite who bought into the theory of photons, then the concept of moving light is actually just moving photons to you, as such you can change light into dark with only Forces 2 since you're just moving photons around (but the very concept of moving &quot;darkness&quot; doesn't really make any kind of sense, so you can't do it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think what you said breaks the whole \u201cEveryone plays by the same rules\u201d concept. I don\u2019t agree with forcing players to have to use different levels of sphere that can be accomplished with lower level spheres, but that is me.<br /> <br /> Like the forces thing. The character can believe they are changing the energies of darkness into light, but the player and ST know they are just doing a Forces 2 effect. And with the entropy thing, the characters can believe it is happening for whatever reason they want, but it is all still an Entropy 1 effect.<br /> <br /> However, if the character doesn\u2019t believe they can move shadows, then they can have Forces 5 and not move shadows. I don\u2019t mean to imply that mechanics working differently doesn\u2019t mean that a character can\u2019t be restricted from a mechanic. If they believe they can move shadows, however they want to explain it (aliens most likely), then they do it with forces 2. If they don\u2019t believe it, they don\u2019t do it.<br /> <br /> Now, even tho you and I have different ways on how we let spheres work, I still think your methodology doesn\u2019t break the \u201ceveryone plays by the same rules\u201d thing (perhaps it bends it, but not breaks). Where <u>I look at the final effect</u> to determine sphere rankings, it appears (at least to me from what I read above) that <u>you look at what they are actually manipulating in the world</u>. And that is also a cool way to look at it, I never really thought of it that way.<br /> <br /> My issue about paradigm changing mechanics takes place when they make the game harder for a character with an interesting concept vs another character with a similar, but different, concept. If we continue this \u2018Mind is now needed for a pyromancer\u2019 then let\u2019s say we have a character who believes there is life in nature. So if that mage wants to manipulate a rock she/he now needs to add Life to do a Matter effect on the rock.<br /> <br /> This, I don\u2019t feel would be fair to the player. The character can believe all day long they are coxing the life in the rock to make it shake, but the player and ST should be cool that this is totally a Matter effect. By forcing them to add Life to the spell, the storyteller just made it easier to counter magick. Setting metagaming aside, why would a player want to limit their game like that? If I was the player, I would just change my paradigm to something a little more basic so I don\u2019t have to worry about adding in spheres I really don\u2019t need.<br /> <br /> But now I wouldn\u2019t restrict a player that wants to add in Life (without me forcing it) because it fits their paradigm. The bonus is with unweaving, and I think that would really eff with future mages that try to undo the spell. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T19:42:41-07:00","id":976892,"title":"","content":"The game sort of requires us to be creative with source material for ex nihilo casting, such as conjuring fire from nothing, unless you use Prime as your source. This is the kind of thing that gives me pause when it comes to mind powers such as telekinesis and pyrokinesis, since they can so easily skirt around the necessity for instruments in casting. It's easy to say that if you use Mind that you're transmuting thoughts or brainpower into Forces energy, but there's no real cost there, where a Hermetic or an Etherite needs to jump through their more inconvenient paradigmatic loops.<br /> <br /> For that reason, I'm kind of on board with the idea that if you use some kind of psychic power to cast your non-Mind effects, there needs to be some kind of price to pay, something to level the playing field with the other mages. I'm not sure how to balance 2 dot powers like minor manipulations, but for summoning, I think that there should be an expenditure of Willpower points per spell. To take the theme even further, one could maybe even temporarily burn dots in Abilities, since you're using your &quot;thoughts.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T21:33:28-07:00","id":976939,"title":"","content":"I have ruled it, in my game, that the HDYDT Pyrokinesis is a bit more controlled and is a way for the Mage to roll one Arete roll for a scene of special powers with fire... making willpower rolls when trying to do outlandish things, but going with the results of the arete roll to rough in any effects that seem in line with paradigm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12296-gabryl","name":"Gabryl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:45:59-07:00","id":977121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976327-pyrokenesis?p=976892#post976892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game sort of requires us to be creative with source material for ex nihilo casting, such as conjuring fire from nothing, unless you use Prime as your source. This is the kind of thing that gives me pause when it comes to mind powers such as telekinesis and pyrokinesis, since they can so easily skirt around the necessity for instruments in casting. It's easy to say that if you use Mind that you're transmuting thoughts or brainpower into Forces energy, but there's no real cost there, where a Hermetic or an Etherite needs to jump through their more inconvenient paradigmatic loops.<br /> <br /> For that reason, I'm kind of on board with the idea that if you use some kind of psychic power to cast your non-Mind effects, there needs to be some kind of price to pay, something to level the playing field with the other mages. I'm not sure how to balance 2 dot powers like minor manipulations, but for summoning, I think that there should be an expenditure of Willpower points per spell. To take the theme even further, one could maybe even temporarily burn dots in Abilities, since you're using your &quot;thoughts.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My preferred method for dealing with this problem is insisting on some kind of knowledge or skill roll, Meditation seems like a good choice, Willpower expenditure, as you say, also works well, although it's a hefty price if it's on a per spell basis. Even more than leveling the playing field, I think it is important for the players to know that their character is really doing something, rather than just wishing really hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}